  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking issue** in `tag-cloud` vs `main`:\n\n**[P1] `topTags` mutates its input, corrupting the sidebar’s recent strip** — `src/tags.js:10`\n`tags.sort(...)` reorders the caller’s array in place. `sidebar()` calls it before reading `tags.slice(0, 5)`, so “recent” becomes the five highest-count tags rather than the first five tags supplied. This also violates the README’s explicit non-mutation contract.\n\nI reproduced it with six tags: the sixth tag moved into the recent strip because of its higher count, displacing the first tag. Sort a copy instead, and add regression tests for input preservation and recent-strip order.\n\n**Validation:** All four existing tests pass, but none checks this behavior. Reviewed through commit `89f074f`. No files changed.",
